WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.669 --> 00:00:08.170
Over 15 years into its run, NCIS has had members
of the team kidnapped, shot, stabbed and even

00:00:08.170 --> 00:00:13.020
blown up by terrorists — but one of the
most shocking deaths came just two seasons

00:00:13.020 --> 00:00:14.020
in.

00:00:14.020 --> 00:00:19.090
Here's the real reason Sasha Alexander, who
portrayed Kate Todd, left NCIS after season 2.

00:00:19.866 --> 00:00:24.680
We know the NCIS team works long hours to
catch the bad guys, but the people who make

00:00:24.680 --> 00:00:29.460
the show are also pulling very long shifts,
purely in the name of entertainment.

00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:34.469
This detail slipped by fans, who were so furious
when Todd was killed off that show creator

00:00:34.469 --> 00:00:37.690
Don Bellisario weighed in on what happened
behind the scenes.

00:00:37.690 --> 00:00:41.700
He explained that he'd already started working
on the script for the last episode of the

00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:44.940
season when Alexander begged him to write
her out of the show.

00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:49.929
In July 2005, a couple of months after Todd's
dramatic death aired, Bellisario shed some

00:00:49.929 --> 00:00:53.890
light on the situation in a conversation with
the Chicago Tribune, saying,

00:00:53.890 --> 00:00:59.459
"Sasha came in two days before I was to leave,
and with tears in her eyes, she said, 'I just

00:00:59.459 --> 00:01:00.879
can't work this hard.'"

00:01:00.879 --> 00:01:05.000
The showrunner admitted that NCIS is, quote,
"a hard show to make.

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:06.680
We work very long hours."

00:01:06.680 --> 00:01:11.820
He also added that although Alexander was
technically under contract to CBS, he persuaded

00:01:11.820 --> 00:01:13.600
the network's brass to let her go.

00:01:13.600 --> 00:01:18.799
While Bellisario and Alexander knew what was
coming, no one else knew about her departure.

00:01:18.799 --> 00:01:23.560
Fans got wind that one of the NCIS team was
going to die in the season two finale.

00:01:23.560 --> 00:01:28.859
But exactly who it would be was kept so secret
that they reportedly even shot an alternate

00:01:28.859 --> 00:01:30.299
ending where Todd survived.

00:01:30.299 --> 00:01:32.249
"We're NCIS agents, McGee.

00:01:32.249 --> 00:01:35.810
There is a chance one of us might die every
time we walk through that door."

00:01:36.979 --> 00:01:41.189
Bellisario isn't the only one to ever lend
credence to the idea that working on NCIS

00:01:41.189 --> 00:01:44.179
could be taxing to the point of exhaustion
for some of his stars.

00:01:44.179 --> 00:01:49.840
Mark Harmon, who has portrayed Special Agent
Leroy Jethro Gibbs on the series for 17 grueling

00:01:49.840 --> 00:01:54.999
years, has spoken in the past not only about
how difficult a gig "NCIS" can be, but about

00:01:54.999 --> 00:01:58.119
how it used to be even more so early in the
series' run.

00:01:58.119 --> 00:02:02.180
During the series' 16th season, Harmon had
a chat with Entertainment Tonight in which

00:02:02.180 --> 00:02:06.490
he acknowledged that the job isn't exactly
a walk in the park, saying,

00:02:06.490 --> 00:02:07.829
"This is hard to do.

00:02:07.829 --> 00:02:11.730
And we miss that sometimes, because this is
a happy group and we all work hard.

00:02:11.730 --> 00:02:14.390
But this looks so much easier than it is.

00:02:14.390 --> 00:02:18.450
And that's because you've got such talented
people in so many different directions here,

00:02:18.450 --> 00:02:21.560
who all get in the same path of what they're
trying to do."

00:02:21.560 --> 00:02:25.620
In a 2017 interview with "The Talk," Harmon
described the early days of the series in

00:02:25.620 --> 00:02:29.720
terms that suggest a schedule that was nothing
short of brutal, saying,

00:02:29.720 --> 00:02:31.940
"The first day was 21 hours.

00:02:31.940 --> 00:02:37.709
We've, I think, maneuvered the [schedule]
over the years to make it much more specific,

00:02:37.709 --> 00:02:39.260
and I think we've gotten better with that."

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:44.110
It's interesting to consider that the character
of Kate Todd might have been a longer-lived

00:02:44.110 --> 00:02:46.629
one, had producers gone with their initial
choice for the role.

00:02:46.629 --> 00:02:50.980
In a conversation with CBS News, Harmon revealed
that Lauren Holly, who portrayed Director

00:02:50.980 --> 00:02:56.030
Jenny Shepard on NCIS from seasons 3 to 5,
almost landed the part before it was handed

00:02:56.030 --> 00:02:57.030
to Alexander.

00:02:57.030 --> 00:03:00.760
"At the time that Sasha was hired, Lauren
was in that mix to play that role.

00:03:00.760 --> 00:03:05.160
And the fact that her name came back up again
for the role of Jenny Shepard did not surprise

00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:07.879
me a lot... because of what [Holly] has as
an actress."

00:03:07.879 --> 00:03:12.850
Holly must have boundless energy, because
when asked why she chose to depart the series

00:03:12.850 --> 00:03:17.129
after only three seasons, she gave a much
different reason: she wanted to take on different

00:03:17.129 --> 00:03:20.340
roles, and was unhappy at Bellisario's departure
from the show.

00:03:20.340 --> 00:03:22.170
On her personal website, Holly wrote,

00:03:22.170 --> 00:03:26.180
"I was saddened that Don Bellisario was forced
out, and I missed him a lot.

00:03:26.180 --> 00:03:30.829
To be honest, now that the work bug had bitten
me again, I got bored with my part of the

00:03:30.829 --> 00:03:31.829
'Director.'

00:03:31.829 --> 00:03:34.379
Then the decision was made to kill me, and
boy did they.

00:03:34.379 --> 00:03:35.829
About five different ways!"

00:03:36.860 --> 00:03:40.590
Fortunately, it seems that Alexander is more
than happy with her decision to leave.

00:03:40.590 --> 00:03:45.260
In a 2012 interview with "TV Guide," she reiterated
that she only left because she personally

00:03:45.260 --> 00:03:46.819
couldn't handle the long hours.

00:03:46.819 --> 00:03:51.470
"People don't realize that on a network show,
you make 24 episodes a year — that's ten-and-a-half

00:03:51.470 --> 00:03:54.310
months a year, 17 hours a day.

00:03:54.310 --> 00:03:55.340
It's hard core."

00:03:55.340 --> 00:03:59.780
Alexander wasn't just thinking about the show's
impact on her work/life balance at the time.

00:03:59.780 --> 00:04:00.780
She added,

00:04:00.780 --> 00:04:04.200
"I really firmly believe in my heart that
I would not be where I am today.

00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:07.799
I didn't want to wake up and be in my forties
and go, 'Oh, my gosh!'

00:04:07.799 --> 00:04:08.980
But people don't understand."

00:04:08.980 --> 00:04:13.689
Taking the risk and leaving NCIS did seem
to pay off personally and professionally.

00:04:13.689 --> 00:04:18.780
Two years after her dramatic exit, Alexander
married Italian director Edoardo Ponti.

00:04:18.780 --> 00:04:22.980
The couple now have two children, and she
also gained a famous mother-in-law: none other

00:04:22.980 --> 00:04:25.330
than iconic actress Sophia Loren.

00:04:25.330 --> 00:04:30.600
Career-wise, Alexander went on to play half
of crime-solving double act "Rizzoli &amp; Isles"

00:04:30.600 --> 00:04:34.440
for seven seasons, and appeared in the Showtime
comedy series "Shameless."

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:38.970
Todd may have taken one for the NCIS team
— but Alexander is happy that she's no longer

00:04:38.970 --> 00:04:41.860
sacrificing her real life for the screen.

